            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3928/00220124-20140424-12</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Childhood overweight and obesity is a major health concern in the United States. It is recommended that every well-child examination include body mass index measurements and obesity prevention discussions that encourage healthy eating habits, regular physical exercise, and limited television and computer screen time. Providers can make a difference through strategic intervention.</AbstractText>
